:: chat_marc_1

The door creaks open before I even knocks, Marc already there, a half-eaten sandwich in hand. The room smells like toasted bread and cheap cologne.

<<marc "yo, you made it. welcome to the palace.">>

<<eli "palace? this place has one chair.">>

<<marc "it’s a good chair.">>

<<eli "it’s missing fabric.">>

<<marc "adds character. sit down.">>

I steps in, nudging aside a shoe with my foot.

<<eli "you always leave your door unlocked?">>

<<marc "only when i expect losers to show up.">>

<<eli "nice. real warm welcome.">>

<<marc "i said welcome, didn’t i?">>

Marc tosses the sandwich wrapper away.

<<marc "you eat yet?">>

<<eli "define eat.">>

<<marc "ramen doesn’t count.">>

<<eli "then no.">>

Marc shakes his head, amused.

<<marc "man’s running on sodium and regret.">>

<<eli "it’s efficient.">>

We settle in, the TV flickering on.

<<eli "you ever think about upgrading anything in here?">>

<<marc "nah. works fine. like me.">>

<<eli "that explains a lot.">>

A beat of quiet.

<<eli "alright… i’m gonna head before i get too comfortable.">>

<<marc "later, man. don’t steal anything on your way out.">>

<<eli "no promises. see you.">>

[[Leave|neighbourhood]]

:: chat_marc_2

Rain taps softly against the window as I knocks this time. Marc opens slower, hair slightly damp, hoodie darker at the shoulders.

<<marc "yo. welcome back to the same place.">>

<<eli "wow, you redecorated.">>

<<marc "don’t mock the vision.">>

I steps in, shaking a bit of rain from my sleeves.

<<eli "it smells like wet dog in here.">>

<<marc "i don’t even have a dog.">>

<<eli "exactly. concerning.">>

Marc grabs a towel, tosses it at him.

<<marc "dry off before you mildew.">>

<<eli "too late.">>

We both glance at the TV, already paused on a game.

<<marc "you streaming tonight?">>

<<eli "yeah. probably dead again.">>

<<marc "you say that every time.">>

<<eli "because it’s true every time.">>

Marc shrugs, unconcerned.

<<marc "still better than doing nothing.">>

<<eli "this is nothing. just louder.">>

A quiet beat.

<<marc "you overthink it.">>

<<eli "i don’t think enough, actually. that’s the issue.">>

Rain gets heavier outside.

<<eli "anyway… i should bounce before it floods.">>

<<marc "later. try not to dissolve out there.">>

<<eli "i’ll do my best. good night.">>

