:: chat_marc_3

Marc opens the door mid-yawn, stretching as I walks in. The apartment smells like instant noodles and something faintly burnt.

<<marc "yo… welcome. ignore the smell.">>

<<eli "what did you do?">>

<<marc "experiment. didn’t work.">>

I eyes the kitchen corner.

<<eli "you almost set this place on fire again?">>

<<marc "almost doesn’t count.">>

<<eli "it absolutely counts.">>

Marc drops onto the couch.

<<marc "you look worse than usual.">>

<<eli "thanks.">>

<<marc "no, like… extra tired.">>

<<eli "yeah. stayed up editing clips.">>

Marc raises a brow.

<<marc "you hate editing.">>

<<eli "i hate everything. might as well try.">>

maybe something sticks… anything. Marc tosses him a drink.

<<marc "you’re trying. that’s new.">>

<<eli "don’t get used to it.">>

We sit in silence for a moment.

<<marc "clips might help though.">>

<<eli "yeah. or they disappear like everything else.">>

Marc shrugs.

<<marc "then you make more.">>

I exhales.

<<eli "i’ll see.">>

He stands after a bit.

<<eli "alright… i’m out. before i inhale whatever that smell is.">>

<<marc "later. i’ll perfect it next time.">>

<<eli "please don’t. bye.">>

